==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro}} ''[[blestre]]''.

===Pronunciation===
*: {{rhymes|ɪstə(r)}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A small [[bubble]] between the layers of the [[skin]] that contains watery or bloody fluid and is caused by [[friction]] and pressure, [[burn]]ing, freezing, chemical irritation, disease or [[infect]]ion.
# A swelling on a plant.
# A bubble, as on a painted surface.
# {{context|roofing}} An [[enclosed]] pocket of air, which may be mixed with water or [[solvent]] [[vapor]], trapped between [[impermeable]] layers of felt or between the [[membrane]] and [[substrate]].

====Synonyms====
* [[bleb]]
* [[bulla]]

====Derived terms====
* [[blister pack]]

